# PATTERN 3: ASYNC HTTP APIs
# The report takes ~24 seconds (3 steps × 8s). Send step 1, then step 3 a few times.

# URL and keys come from http-client.env.json. Local values are the default; to test the deployed app, choose azure at the top right of this editor.

### 1. Start the report → 202 Accepted + Location header + management URLs
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports
x-functions-key: {{functionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportId": "q3-emea",
  "region": "EMEA",
  "from": "2026-07-01",
  "to": "2026-09-30"
}

### 2. Send the exact same request again → same instance ID, no second report (idempotent start)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports
x-functions-key: {{functionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportId": "q3-emea",
  "region": "EMEA",
  "from": "2026-07-01",
  "to": "2026-09-30"
}

### 3. Your own status endpoint: 202 + Retry-After while running, 200 + DownloadUrl when done
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/q3-emea
x-functions-key: {{functionKey}}

### 4. The built-in status endpoint (what StatusQueryGetUri points to), for comparison
GET {{hostUrl}}/runtime/webhooks/durabletask/instances/report-q3-emea?code={{systemKey}}
